<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr" class="no-js">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>Nova Design System</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<style>
@font-face{font-family:"Vazirmatn";src:url(assets/fonts/vazirmatn-Regular-fa.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:400;font-display:swap}
@font-face{font-family:"Vazirmatn";src:url(assets/fonts/vazirmatn-Bold-fa.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:700;font-display:swap}
@font-face{font-family:"Vazirmatn";src:url(assets/fonts/vazirmatn-Regular-latin.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:400;font-display:swap;unicode-range:U+0041-005A,U+0061-007A}
@font-face{font-family:"Vazirmatn";src:url(assets/fonts/vazirmatn-Bold-latin.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:700;font-display:swap;unicode-range:U+0041-005A,U+0061-007A}
@font-face{font-family:"JetBrains Mono";src:url(assets/fonts/jbmono-400.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:400;font-display:swap}
@font-face{font-family:"JetBrains Mono";src:url(assets/fonts/jbmono-600.woff2) format("woff2");font-weight:600;font-display:swap}
</style>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/nova.css">
<style>
.ds { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 48px; align-items: start; padding-block: 32px 96px; }
.ds-nav { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--bar-h) + 16px); display: grid; gap: 2px; font-size: .875rem; }
.ds-nav a { color: var(--ink-2); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 0; border-inline-start: 2px solid transparent; padding-inline-start: 10px; }
.ds-nav a:hover { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--line); }
.ds-nav b { font-size: .6875rem; color: var(--ink-3); font-family: var(--mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 12px 0 4px; }
.ds main > section { padding-block: 40px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--line); }
.ds main > section:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
.ds h2 { font-size: var(--fs-3); margin-bottom: 8px; }
.ds h3 { font-size: var(--fs-1); margin: 28px 0 10px; }
.ds p.lead { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 70ch; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.ds-rules { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-3); border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--line-3); }
.ds-rules > div { padding: 16px; border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--line-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); }
.ds-rules b { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.ds-rules span { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .9375rem; }
.sw { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
.sw div { border: 1px solid var(--line-3); background: var(--sheet); font-size: .75rem; }
.sw i { display: block; height: 52px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); }
.sw span { display: block; padding: 6px 8px; line-height: 1.4; }
.sw code { color: var(--ink-3); }
.tbl-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
.tbl { width: 100%; font-size: .875rem; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--line); }
.tbl th, .tbl td { text-align: start; padding: 8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); vertical-align: top; }
.tbl thead th { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 400; }
.tbl td.r { text-align: end; font-family: var(--mono); white-space: nowrap; }
.ok { color: var(--ok); } .warn { color: var(--pending); }
.spec-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); }
.spec-row small { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--ink-3); font-size: .6875rem; }
.pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
.pair > * { min-width: 0; }
.pane { border: 1px dashed var(--line-2); padding: 16px; background: var(--paper); }
.pane > small { display: block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .6875rem; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 10px; }
.stack { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
.space { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
.space div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .75rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
.space i { display: block; height: 10px; background: var(--tint-2); }
.gridshow { position: relative; height: 120px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: var(--col-gap); }
.gridshow i { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tint-2) 45%, transparent); border-inline: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
.glyphs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--line-3); border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--line-3); }
.glyphs div { padding: 14px; border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--line-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); font-size: .75rem; color: var(--ink-2); display: grid; gap: 6px; justify-items: start; }
.glyphs svg { width: 96px; height: 72px; color: var(--line); }
.mini-ws { border: 1.5px solid var(--line); background: var(--sheet); }
.icons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }
.icons span { display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: 4px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .625rem; color: var(--ink-3); width: 64px; }
.icons svg { width: 24px; height: 24px; color: var(--ink); }
@media (max-width: 899px) { .ds { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } .ds-nav { display: none; } .pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .glyphs { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{% include "symbols.svg.j2" %}
<aside class="proto" aria-label="Prototype"><div class="wrap"><span>Phase 2 V2 · Design system v0.3 · for Gate 2 review</span><a href="./">Review hub</a></div></aside>
<header class="bar navy"><div class="wrap bar__in">
  <a class="brand" href="./"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#logo"/></svg><span><b>Nova design system</b><small>Polad Charkhesh · v0.3</small></span></a>
  <nav class="bar__nav" aria-label="Prototypes"><a href="fa.html" lang="fa">نسخه فارسی</a><a href="en.html">English prototype</a><a href="admin.html">Admin wireframes</a></nav>
</div></header>
<div class="wrap ds">
<nav class="ds-nav" aria-label="Design system sections">
  <b>Foundations</b><a href="#principles">Principles</a><a href="#color">Colour and surfaces</a><a href="#type">Typography</a><a href="#space">Spacing and grid</a><a href="#shape">Lines, shape, elevation</a>
  <b>Language</b><a href="#drawing">Technical drawing</a><a href="#bidi">Persian RTL / English LTR</a>
  <b>Components</b><a href="#controls">Controls</a><a href="#data">Data display</a><a href="#explorer">Explorer and workspace</a><a href="#forms">Forms and contact</a>
  <b>Behaviour</b><a href="#motion">Motion and reduced motion</a><a href="#perf">Performance ledger</a>
</nav>
<main>

<h1 class="sr">Nova design system v0.3</h1>
<section id="principles">
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <p class="lead">The website is a numbered set of engineering drawings. Every visual rule below exists either because engineers already read it that way, or because it keeps the page fast on a weak connection.</p>
  <div class="ds-rules">
    <div><b>Drawing, not decoration</b><span>Graphics follow drafting conventions (line types, sections, dimensions, balloons, title blocks) and are generated from product data wherever possible.</span></div>
    <div><b>Paper for reading, navy for moments</b><span>Data and reading happen on paper sheets. Deep navy fields mark the moments of the story: find (hero), understand (Anatomy), talk (contact) and the footer that closes it.</span></div>
    <div><b>Every colour has one job</b><span>Brand navy is ink and action on paper; icy blue is interaction and focus; pale ice is the action on navy; steel is only for rendering metal; brass is the one warm accent and marks "the part in focus"; amber is only for pending data.</span></div>
    <div><b>Metal only where it is the product</b><span>Restrained metallic gradients appear only on bearing renderings (hero, assembled state, closing mark). UI chrome has no glass, glow, blur or shadow.</span></div>
    <div><b>Codes are sacred</b><span>Part codes, dimensions, units, drawing references and phone numbers use Latin digits, isolated left-to-right, in both languages. Persian prose and ordinary counts use Persian digits.</span></div>
    <div><b>Honest data, weight as input</b><span>Verified and pending are always visible. Every visual decision has a byte and CPU cost, listed in the performance ledger at the end of this page.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="color">
  <h2>Colour and surfaces</h2>
  <p class="lead">Fixed brand and material constants, then one semantic token set in three contexts: Light (default), Dark (follows the device setting, no toggle) and the Navy field (<code>.navy</code>: hero, Anatomy, contact and footer, in both themes). Values below are read from <code>nova.css</code>, so this page cannot drift from the code.</p>
  <h3>Brand and material constants</h3>
  <div class="sw">{% for k, v, role in constants %}<div><i style="background:{{ v }}"></i><span><b>--{{ k }}</b><br><code>{{ v }}</code><br>{{ role }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div>
  {% for name, pal in palettes %}
  <h3>{{ name }}</h3>
  <div class="sw">{% for k, v, role in pal %}<div><i style="background:{{ v }}"></i><span><b>--{{ k }}</b><br><code>{{ v }}</code><br>{{ role }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div>
  {% endfor %}
  <h3>Contrast, measured (WCAG 2.1)</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Use</th><th class="r">Light</th><th class="r">Dark</th><th class="r">Navy field</th><th>Needs</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for row in contrast %}<tr><td><code>{{ row[0] }}</code></td><td>{{ row[1] }}</td>{% for v in row[2] %}<td class="r {{ 'ok' if v >= row[3] else 'warn' }}">{{ '%.1f'|format(v) }}:1</td>{% endfor %}<td>{{ row[3] }}:1</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Surface hierarchy</h3>
  <div class="spec-row"><small>--paper</small><span>The page. Sections sit directly on it, separated by rules, not by boxes.</span></div>
  <div class="spec-row"><small>--paper-2</small><span>Recessed: hover rows, the drawing frame inside the band.</span></div>
  <div class="spec-row"><small>--sheet</small><span>Raised: inputs, the product workspace, title blocks, drawing frames. Always with a border; never with a shadow.</span></div>
  <div class="spec-row"><small>.navy</small><span>A whole section re-tokened to deep navy: paper becomes navy, ink becomes near-white, the action becomes pale ice with navy text, the accent becomes light brass. Components inside need no special cases.</span></div>
  <div class="spec-row"><small>metal</small><span>Steel gradients (<code>--steel-*</code>) and a brass cage are allowed only inside bearing renderings. Never on buttons, cards or backgrounds.</span></div>
</section>

<section id="type">
  <h2>Typography</h2>
  <p class="lead">Two families, two weights each, subset per language and self-hosted. Persian pages load {{ fonts.fa_total }} KB of fonts; English pages {{ fonts.en_total }} KB.</p>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Used on</th><th class="r">Size</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for f in fonts.files %}<tr><td><code>{{ f[0] }}</code></td><td>{{ f[1] }}</td><td>{{ f[2] }}</td><td class="r">{{ f[3] }} KB</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  <tr><td colspan="3" class="muted">For comparison: Vazirmatn full static Regular 50.7 KB; full variable font 111 KB; variable subset 47.7 KB; JetBrains Mono Latin with ligatures 21.2 KB.</td><td></td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Scale (ratio ≈ 1.25, display sizes fluid)</h3>
  {% for tok, px, fa_s, en_s, w in scale %}
  <div class="spec-row"><small>--{{ tok }} · {{ px }}</small><div class="pair"><span lang="fa" dir="rtl" style="font-size:var(--{{ tok }});font-weight:{{ w }};line-height:var(--lh-h)">{{ fa_s }}</span><span lang="en" style="font-size:var(--{{ tok }});font-weight:{{ w }};line-height:var(--lh-h)">{{ en_s }}</span></div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="spec-row"><small>mono · codes</small><div class="pair"><span class="mono" style="font-size:1.875rem;font-weight:600">22220 E</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:1rem">25 × 52 × 15 mm · Ø180 · n lim</span></div></div>
  <h3>Rules</h3>
  <div class="ds-rules">
    <div><b>Line height</b><span>Persian body 1.85, headings 1.45 (tall ascenders and descenders). English body 1.6, headings 1.15.</span></div>
    <div><b>No letter-spacing on Persian</b><span>Tracking breaks cursive joins. Uppercase and tracking are for Latin labels and mono captions only.</span></div>
    <div><b>Digits</b><span>Latin in both languages for codes, dimensions, units, drawing references and phone numbers (<span class="mono">6205-2RS · 25 mm · PC-04-A · 0912 719 5313</span>). Persian prose and ordinary counts use Persian digits (<span lang="fa">۱۳ محصول</span>).</span></div>
    <div><b>Dates</b><span>Persian pages show the Solar Hijri calendar (<span lang="fa">۱۲ مهر ۱۴۰۵</span>) via <code>Intl</code> in the browser or PHP <code>intl</code> at publish; English pages show 4 Oct 2026.</span></div>
    <div><b>Fallbacks and preload</b><span>Segoe UI, Tahoma and system fonts behind Vazirmatn; <code>font-display: swap</code>. The Bold weight is preloaded because the hero headline is the LCP element.</span></div>
    <div><b>Minimum size</b><span>No UI label below 13 px (<code>--fs--2</code>). Running text stays within 50–70 characters; headings use <code>text-wrap: balance</code>.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="space">
  <h2>Spacing and grid</h2>
  <p class="lead">A 4 px base. Layout spacing comes from grid gaps, never from margins on individual blocks.</p>
  <div class="space">{% for k, v in spacing %}<div><span>--{{ k }} {{ v }}</span><i style="width:{{ v }}"></i></div>{% endfor %}</div>
  <h3>Grid</h3>
  <p class="lead">12 columns, max width 1280 px, gutter clamp(16 px, 4vw, 48 px), column gap clamp(16 px, 2.4vw, 32 px). The hero splits 6 / 6. The overlay below is the live grid at this window size.</p>
  <div class="gridshow" aria-hidden="true">{% for i in range(12) %}<i></i>{% endfor %}</div>
  <h3>Breakpoints (where layout actually changes)</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Width</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td class="mono">≥ 1100</td><td>Catalogue table + 440 px docked workspace; families in 5 columns; hero two columns.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">900–1099</td><td>Workspace narrows to 320–380 px; families in 2 columns.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">&lt; 900</td><td>Mobile mode: header menu, bottom action dock (Call · WhatsApp · Search), hero stacks with the search inside the first viewport, workspace becomes a bottom sheet, Anatomy stacks with a numbers-only stage strip.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">&lt; 700</td><td>Catalogue rows become two-line records (code + status / family / d × D × B); the ask panel stacks.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">&lt; 600</td><td>Sheet heads drop the tick ruler and reference; forms go single-column.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section id="shape">
  <h2>Lines, shape and elevation</h2>
  <div class="ds-rules">
    <div><b>Radius 2 px</b><span>Drawing sheets have square corners. The only round things are bearings, balloons and status dots.</span></div>
    <div><b>1.5 px structural</b><span>Section rules, sheet heads, inputs, the workspace frame, the action dock.</span></div>
    <div><b>1 px dividers</b><span>Rows, cells, title-block partitions.</span></div>
    <div><b>Dashed means "not final"</b><span>Pending data, empty states, example chips. Never used for decoration.</span></div>
    <div><b>No shadows, blur or glow</b><span>Elevation comes from surface colour plus a border; gradients exist only as metal inside bearing renderings. This also keeps painting cheap on low-end phones.</span></div>
    <div><b>Focus</b><span>2 px signal-blue outline, 2 px offset, on every interactive element.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="drawing">
  <h2>Technical drawing language</h2>
  <p class="lead">Simplified ISO 128-style conventions. Drawings are never mirrored on Persian pages and always read left to right.</p>
  <figure class="dwg" style="margin:0">
    <svg class="dwg-svg draw" viewBox="0 0 760 250" role="img" aria-label="Line conventions">
      <g font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="11" style="fill:var(--ink-3)">
        <text x="20" y="34">OBJECT 1.5</text><path class="ln-obj" data-d pathLength="1" d="M130 30H330"/>
        <text x="20" y="64">THIN 0.9</text><path class="ln-thin" d="M130 60H330"/>
        <text x="20" y="94">HIDDEN</text><path class="ln-hid" d="M130 90H330"/>
        <text x="20" y="124">CENTRE</text><path class="ln-ctr" d="M130 120H330"/>
        <text x="20" y="164">DIMENSION</text><path class="ln-dim" d="M150 140V178M310 140V178"/><path class="ln-dim" d="M150 170H310" marker-start="url(#ar)" marker-end="url(#ar)"/><text class="dim-t" x="230" y="164" text-anchor="middle">Ø52</text>
        <text x="20" y="214">SECTION</text><rect class="fill-sec" x="150" y="196" width="160" height="30"/>
        <text x="400" y="34">LEADER + BALLOON</text>
      </g>
      <g class="balloon"><path class="ln-thin" d="M470 120L520 70"/><circle cx="532" cy="58" r="13"/><text x="532" y="62.5">3</text></g>
      <circle class="fill-paper" cx="470" cy="128" r="14"/>
      <g font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="11" style="fill:var(--ink-3)"><text x="600" y="34">STATUS</text></g>
      <rect x="600" y="50" width="130" height="26" style="fill:var(--ok-bg);stroke:var(--ok)"/><text x="614" y="67" font-size="12" style="fill:var(--ok)">■ Verified</text>
      <rect x="600" y="88" width="130" height="26" style="fill:var(--pending-bg);stroke:var(--pending-line);stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="614" y="105" font-size="12" style="fill:var(--pending)">◌ Pending</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption><span>LINE TYPES · SECTION HATCH · BALLOONS</span><span>NTS</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h3>Sheet head and title block</h3>
  {{ sheethead(3, 'Product explorer') }}
  <dl class="tblock" style="--cols:4"><div><dt>Company</dt><dd>Polad Charkhesh</dd></div><div><dt>Address</dt><dd>No. 433, Dardasht St, Narmak, Tehran</dd></div><div><dt>Working hours</dt><dd>08:00–16:00</dd></div><div><dt>Landline</dt><dd class="num">021 7720 9117</dd></div></dl>
  <h3>Family glyphs (schematic half-sections, one <code>&lt;symbol&gt;</code> each, reused by <code>&lt;use&gt;</code>)</h3>
  <div class="glyphs">{% for f in families %}<div><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ f.glyph }}"/></svg><b>{{ f.en }}</b><span lang="fa">{{ f.fa }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div>
  <h3>Generated product drawings</h3>
  <p class="lead">Each product's section drawing is built from its boundary dimensions (d, D, B/T/C/H) with the family's template, so a drawing exists even before any photo. Open any product in the prototypes to see one. In production the Publish Engine renders the SVG into the product's HTML.</p>
</section>

<section id="bidi">
  <h2>Persian RTL / English LTR</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Mirror</th><th>Never mirror</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Page layout, grid order, navigation, the explorer (filters start, workspace end), the Exploded Assembly layout, sticky footers, directional icons (arrows, chevrons, send).</td><td>Technical drawings, dimension text, part codes, numbers inside codes, units, phone numbers (isolated LTR), the logo mark, the decoder breakdown order.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Mechanics</h3>
  <div class="ds-rules">
    <div><b>Logical properties only</b><span><code>margin-inline</code>, <code>inset-inline-start</code>, <code>border-inline-end</code>, <code>text-align: start</code>; no left/right in the stylesheet except inside drawings.</span></div>
    <div><b>Isolate, don't flip blocks</b><span>Codes sit in <code>&lt;bdi dir="ltr"&gt;</code> inside an RTL block, so they keep their order but align to the start of the Persian line.</span></div>
    <div><b>Inputs</b><span>Search uses <code>dir="auto"</code>: a typed code runs LTR, typed Persian runs RTL; the Persian placeholder is forced RTL and isolates its example code.</span></div>
    <div><b>Search normalisation</b><span>Persian and Arabic digits, Arabic ي/ك, spaces, hyphens, slashes and × are normalised, so typing ۶۲۰۵ (Persian digits) finds 6205.</span></div>
    <div><b>Keyboard</b><span>Arrow keys in the workspace tabs follow reading direction (Left = next in Persian).</span></div>
    <div><b>Latin islands (approved, Gate 2 decision A)</b><span>On Persian pages, technical and utility Latin (codes, units, references, source keys, the EN switch and short English names of three words or fewer) is set in JetBrains Mono, which is already loaded, so the Persian font ships without Latin letters. The rule stays narrow: longer English text on a Persian page (for example a CMS-entered English sentence) takes <code>class="en-prose"</code> and uses the system sans, with no extra download.</span></div>
    <div><b>Codes inside Persian sentences</b><span>Codes inserted into Persian sentences and WhatsApp text are wrapped in Unicode isolates (LRI … PDI), so <span class="mono">6205-2RS</span> never reorders to <span class="mono">2RS-6205</span>. Search strips these marks.</span></div>
    <div><b>Second script on each page</b><span>English pages load a Persian-only subset (11.6 KB) so the brand name and family names in Persian shape correctly.</span></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Same component, both directions</h3>
  <div class="pair">
    {% for L in ['fa', 'en'] %}
    <div class="pane" lang="{{ L }}" dir="{{ 'rtl' if L == 'fa' else 'ltr' }}"><small>{{ L|upper }} · {{ 'RTL' if L == 'fa' else 'LTR' }}</small>
      <table class="cat"><thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr">{{ 'خانواده' if L == 'fa' else 'Family' }}</span></th><th scope="col">{{ 'کد' if L == 'fa' else 'Code' }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'خانواده' if L == 'fa' else 'Family' }}</th><th scope="col" class="n">d</th><th scope="col" class="n">D</th><th scope="col" class="n">B / T</th><th scope="col">{{ 'وضعیت' if L == 'fa' else 'Status' }}</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        {% for p in sample_rows %}<tr><td class="cat__g"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ fam[p.family].glyph }}"/></svg></td><td><a class="cat__code" href="{{ L }}.html#p-{{ p.slug }}"><bdi dir="ltr">{{ p.code }}</bdi></a></td><td class="cat__fam">{{ fam[p.family]['short_' + L] }}</td>{% for k, v in p.cols %}<td class="n{% if not v %} x{% endif %}">{% if v %}{{ v }}{% if k not in ('d', 'D', 'B') %}<sub>{{ k }}</sub>{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td class="dims"><bdi dir="ltr">{{ p.dims_show }}</bdi> <span class="u">mm</span></td><td>{% if p.status == 'verified' %}<span class="badge badge--ok"><span>{{ 'تأییدشده' if L == 'fa' else 'Verified' }}</span></span>{% else %}<span class="badge badge--pending"><span>{{ 'در انتظار تأیید' if L == 'fa' else 'Pending' }}</span></span>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="controls">
  <h2>Controls</h2>
  <h3>Buttons</h3>
  <div class="stack"><a class="btn" href="#controls"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg>Check availability on WhatsApp</a><a class="btn btn--line" href="#controls">Inquiry form</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#controls">Ghost</a><a class="btn btn--line btn--icon" href="#controls" aria-label="Call"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg></a><a class="btn btn--sm" href="#controls">Small</a><a class="btn btn--lg" href="#controls">Large</a><button class="btn" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">One action colour across the site, never a brand green, even for WhatsApp: brand navy on paper, pale ice with navy text on navy fields. Minimum target 44 px (36 px for the small size in dense toolbars).</p>
  <div class="navy" style="padding:20px;margin-top:12px"><div class="stack"><a class="btn" href="#controls"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg>Ask about this code</a><a class="btn btn--line" href="#controls">Inquiry form</a><a class="wa-big" href="#controls" style="max-width:360px"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg><b>{{ t.wa_big }}</b><span>0912 719 5313</span></a></div></div>
  <h3>Hero search (navy field) and explorer search</h3>
  <div class="navy" style="padding:20px"><form class="search search--hero" role="search" aria-label="Hero search specimen" lang="fa" dir="rtl" onsubmit="return false"><span class="search__ico"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-search"/></svg></span><input type="search" dir="auto" aria-label="Hero search specimen" placeholder="کد قطعه، مثلاً &#x2066;6205-2RS&#x2069;"><button type="submit">جستجو</button></form></div>
  <div class="pair" style="margin-top:12px">
    <form class="search" role="search" aria-label="Persian specimen" lang="fa" dir="rtl" onsubmit="return false"><span class="search__ico"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-search"/></svg></span><input type="search" dir="auto" aria-label="Persian specimen" placeholder="کد قطعه، مثلاً &#x2066;6205-2RS&#x2069;"><button type="submit">جستجو</button></form>
    <form class="search" role="search" aria-label="English specimen" onsubmit="return false"><span class="search__ico"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-search"/></svg></span><input type="search" dir="auto" aria-label="English specimen" placeholder="Part code, e.g. 6205-2RS"><button type="submit">Search</button></form>
  </div>
  <h3>Family rail with counts, bore segments, verified toggle</h3>
  <div class="rail" role="group" aria-label="Family specimen"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#g-ball"/></svg><b>All</b><i>13</i></button>{% for f in families[:5] %}<button type="button" aria-pressed="false" {% if not f.count %}disabled{% endif %}><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ f.glyph }}"/></svg><b>{{ f.short_en }}</b><i>{{ f.count }}</i></button>{% endfor %}</div>
  <div class="filters" style="margin-top:10px"><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Bore specimen"><span>d (mm)</span><button type="button" aria-pressed="true">All</button>{% for v, label in t.bores %}<button type="button" aria-pressed="false" dir="ltr">{{ label }}</button>{% endfor %}</div><button class="toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Verified data only</button></div>
  <h3>"Ask about this code" (the query is kept, never a dead end)</h3>
  <div class="ask"><div><p>{{ t.ask_zero.split('{q}')[0] }}<b class="ask__q">6208</b>{{ t.ask_zero.split('{q}')[1] }}</p><p>{{ t.ask_zero_p }}</p></div><div class="ask__acts"><a class="btn" href="#controls"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg>Ask about this code</a><a class="btn btn--line" href="#controls">Inquiry form</a></div></div>
  <h3>Badges, chips, tags</h3>
  <div class="stack"><button class="chip" type="button">6205</button><button class="chip" type="button">22220 E</button>
    <span class="badge badge--ok"><span>Dimensions verified</span></span><span class="badge badge--pending"><span>Technical data pending / Unverified</span></span><a class="tag" href="#controls">Spherical roller bearings</a></div>
  <h3>Icons (1.5 px stroke, 24 grid, one sprite in the page)</h3>
  <div class="icons">{% for i in ['search','close','phone','chat','arrow','chev','copy','link','doc','ext','menu','pin','clock','send'] %}<span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="ico"><use href="#i-{{ i }}"/></svg>{{ i }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
</section>

<section id="data">
  <h2>Data display</h2>
  <div class="pair">
    <div class="pane"><small>SPEC TABLE + SOURCE</small>
      <table class="spec"><caption>Boundary dimensions</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col" class="sym">Symbol</th><th scope="col" class="val">mm</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><th scope="row">Bore diameter</th><td class="sym">d</td><td class="val">25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Outside diameter</th><td class="sym">D</td><td class="val">52</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Width</th><td class="sym">B</td><td class="val">15</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <p class="src"><span>Source:</span><a href="https://www.123bearing.com/bearing-housing/deep-groove-bearing/single-row/6205-skf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">123bearing.com — 6205</a><span>checked 4 Oct 2026 · prototype</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="pane"><small>PENDING DATA</small>
      <div class="pendingbox"><b>Load ratings and speeds</b><span>These values are not yet recorded from a verified source, so none are shown.</span><ul><li>C · Basic dynamic load rating</li><li>C0 · Basic static load rating</li><li>n lim · Limiting speed</li></ul></div>
      <div class="empty" style="margin-top:12px"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg><b>No datasheet published yet</b><span>Empty states say what will appear here and when.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h3>Workspace readout (boundary dimensions at a glance)</h3>
  <div class="ws" style="position:static;max-height:none;max-width:440px"><div class="readout" style="--n:3"><div><small>d · Bore diameter</small><b>25</b><span>mm</span></div><div><small>D · Outside diameter</small><b>52</b><span>mm</span></div><div><small>B · Width</small><b>15</b><span>mm</span></div></div></div>
  <h3>Document row (sample, not real content)</h3>
  <div class="channels" style="max-width:640px"><a href="#data"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg><span><small>PDF · English · 320 KB · 4 Oct 2026</small>Sample datasheet title</span><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-ext"/></svg></a></div>
</section>

<section id="explorer">
  <h2>Explorer and workspace</h2>
  <div class="ds-rules">
    <div><b>A catalogue, not product cards</b><span>A real table: drawing glyph, designation, family, d / D / B (or the family's own symbols), provenance. Every row is a crawlable link; JavaScript only hides rows.</span></div>
    <div><b>Family rail with counts</b><span>Short family names, glyph and count; empty families are disabled rather than hidden, so the range stays visible.</span></div>
    <div><b>Exact match lands on the answer</b><span>Submitting an exact code (or a search with one result) scrolls to the results and opens the workspace with its actions in view.</span></div>
    <div><b>No match keeps the query</b><span>The typed code is carried into "Ask about this code" (WhatsApp) and the inquiry form; a partial match shows a softer version of the same offer.</span></div>
    <div><b>Workspace, desktop</b><span>Docked at the inline end, sticky, no inner page-in-page: designation, d/D/B readout, tabs (Overview · Specifications · Documents), drawing before imagery, and a footer with WhatsApp / Call / Inquiry.</span></div>
    <div><b>Workspace, mobile</b><span>A bottom sheet sized to its content (max 88% height): the page behind is inert; Esc, scrim, drag-down and close all dismiss; focus returns to the row. The dock hides while it is open.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:16px">Try it: <a href="fa.html#p-22220-e" lang="fa">۲۲۲۲۰ E در نسخه فارسی</a> · <a href="en.html#p-ucp-208">UCP 208 (pending data) in English</a></p>
</section>

<section id="forms">
  <h2>Forms and contact</h2>
  <form class="form" style="max-width:720px" novalidate onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="field"><label for="x1">Full name</label><input class="input" id="x1"></div>
    <div class="field is-err"><label for="x2">Phone number</label><input class="input ltr" id="x2" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="x2e"><span class="err" id="x2e">This field is required.</span></div>
    <div class="field field--full"><label for="x3">Part code</label><input class="input ltr" id="x3" placeholder="6205-2RS"><span class="hint">Don't know the code? Leave it empty and describe the application.</span></div>
  </form>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">No price, quantity-based totals or "add to cart" anywhere. The only submit action is "Send inquiry", and WhatsApp sits beside it as an equal alternative.</p>
</section>

<section id="motion">
  <h2>Motion and reduced motion</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td class="mono">--t-fast</td><td class="mono">120ms</td><td>Hover and pressed states</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">--t</td><td class="mono">240ms</td><td>Bottom sheet, scrim</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">--t-slow</td><td class="mono">520ms</td><td>Fallback draw-on</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mono">--ease</td><td class="mono">cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)</td><td>Everything time-based</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Behaviours and their drivers</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Behaviour</th><th>Chrome / Edge, Safari 26+</th><th>Browsers without scroll timelines</th><th>Reduced motion</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><b>Drawing Set</b>: each sheet's line work draws as it enters; the process raceway extends</td><td>CSS <code>view-timeline</code>, no JS</td><td>IntersectionObserver adds <code>.is-drawn</code> once</td><td>Drawn from the start</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Hero bearing</b>: the rolling elements turn a few degrees with scroll and lean toward the pointer</td><td>CSS <code>scroll(root)</code> timeline drives <code>--sr</code>; a rAF-throttled pointer handler sets <code>--pr</code> (fine pointers only)</td><td>Passive scroll listener while the hero is visible</td><td>Static</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Exploded Assembly</b>: one progress value <code>--p</code> drives six stages (table below)</td><td>CSS <code>view-timeline</code> on the track animates the registered <code>--p</code>; everything else is derived in CSS</td><td>One passive scroll listener, active only while the stage is on screen, sets <code>--p</code></td><td>No sticky track; the complete dimensioned technical state, with every balloon and the full parts list</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Workspace sheet</b> (mobile)</td><td colspan="2">240 ms transform, compositor-only</td><td>Instant</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Scroll to explorer</b> after a search</td><td colspan="2">Smooth scroll</td><td>Jump</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Exploded Assembly: six stages from one value</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="r">Progress --p</th><th>What changes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>01 Assembled</td><td class="r">0–0.10</td><td>Metallic rendering, parts together on the shaft</td></tr>
    <tr><td>02 Separated</td><td class="r">0.10–0.30</td><td>Parts slide apart along the axis; metal fades to the hatched technical layer</td></tr>
    <tr><td>03 Dimensioned</td><td class="r">0.30–0.45</td><td>Ød, ØD and B dimensions draw in</td></tr>
    <tr><td>04 Explained</td><td class="r">0.45–0.72</td><td>Balloons 1–6 and parts-list rows light in turn (brass ring + row tint)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>05 Related</td><td class="r">0.72–0.86</td><td>Related product families are underlined in brass; links go to the filtered explorer</td></tr>
    <tr><td>06 Resolved</td><td class="r">0.86–1.00</td><td>Parts reassemble; annotations fade; metal returns</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Desktop track 320 vh; mobile 190 vh with a numbers-only stage strip and the active stage name below it.</p>
  <h3>Live specimen</h3>
  <figure class="dwg" style="margin:0;max-width:520px">{% include "final.svg.j2" %}<figcaption><span>DRAW-ON · SCROLL-DRIVEN</span><span>NTS</span></figcaption></figure>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Rules: only <code>transform</code>, <code>opacity</code> and <code>stroke-dashoffset</code> animate; no parallax; no continuous rotation; nothing waits for animation to become readable; one sticky stage on the whole page.</p>
</section>

<section id="perf">
  <h2>Performance ledger</h2>
  <p class="lead">Measured on this prototype with Chromium, a 390 px phone viewport, 4× CPU slowdown and cache disabled. Numbers are compressed transfer sizes.</p>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Cost</th><th>Measured / effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for r in ledger %}<tr><td>{{ r[0] }}</td><td>{{ r[1] }}</td><td>{{ r[2] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
</section>
</main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
